#4 Problem Statement
Develop a Java program that simulates a Basic Customer Account Management System.
Classes and Their Responsibilities
1. Address Class
•	Attributes: street, city, state, pinCode.
•	Represents a customer’s address.
2. Account Class
•	Attributes: accountNumber, balance.
•	Methods:
o	deposit(double amount)
o	withdraw(double amount)
o	getBalance()
•	Throws a custom exception InsufficientBalanceException when withdrawal would make balance negative.
3. Customer Class
•	Attributes: cid, name, Account account, Address address.
•	Methods:
o	Display full customer details (with account and address info).
4. InsufficientBalanceException
•	A user-defined checked exception triggered during invalid withdrawal.
________________________________________
 Instructions
1.	Create the above four classes in one file (or multiple files if preferred).
2.	Define InsufficientBalanceException as a subclass of Exception.
3.	In the withdraw() method of Account, throw the exception if the withdrawal amount > current balance.
4.	Catch this exception in the main program (inside try-catch).
5.	Demonstrate at least one successful deposit/withdrawal and one failed withdrawal due to insufficient funds.
6.	Display full customer details after operations.
________________________________________
Requirements
•	Use Core Java only (no frameworks).
•	Demonstrate proper use of OOP principles: composition, encapsulation, constructors.
•	Use custom exception handling.
•	Ensure outputs are clearly labeled and formatted.
